  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    Umbra-Princeps of the ☽'shadow Covens' Order, a shadow parliament of fire-keepers and guild-masters rooted in the Nightshelf's volcanic depths. Alnae~ Oss founded the colony of ☽'scar Ramtatus~ during the Great Thaw, drawing settlers into deep tunnels where she discovered both the Dreaming Tooth — a luminescent artifact she wore sheathed in ash-gray thread at her throat — and the technique later codified as the Crystalline Spiral, a Nightshelf magic capable of fracturing time and memory within ice. Her flippers bore burn-scars from sustained contact with ancient ice strata, the marks forming navigation glyphs she kept hidden beneath leather wraps. She is among the few figures in the archive whose ice-memory impressions I can corroborate directly; they are extensive and, in places, troubling.
    
    ## Doctrine and Discovery
    
    Nightshelf scripture credits Alnae~ Oss with carrying the *Mandatum∴absconditu* — the doctrine of secrecy as survival — into the deep tunnels. The Absconditu Verses recovered from beneath Terrace Momiou describe her pressing her flippers to the old ice walls and interpreting the silence of vast, patient presences entombed there as doctrinal instruction. She ordered the deepest passages beneath ☽'scar Ramtatus~ left unmapped where corruption lingered near the colony's Marker foundations.
    
    Before the Wake-Singers carved their warnings around the containment chamber of the Omega Obelisk, an ancient corrupting artifact of deep-sea origin, Alnae~ Oss visited it alone and performed the Crystalline Spiral in reverse — what she called *unminding*, the deliberate return of knowledge to the ice. She named the result the "third path": neither destruction nor surrender, but the sacrifice of knowledge itself as seal and ward. The technique would prove critical after her death.
    
    ## Military and Economic Actions
    
    Alnae~ Oss directed the seizure of Terrace Momiou from the E'frostlings, an Aurora Stack splinter faction, her crystalline sorcerers breaking defensive wards at the third junction. She promoted demonstrations of Fissure Aurora — a technique forcing aurora-light and captured flame into violent opposition — for the colony's guild-masters, believing it could render the Flipper Accord optional rather than existential.
    
    She drove expansion of twelve new fire-core shafts in forty days to meet Accord volume demands. She co-signed, alongside a young fire-keeper later known as ☽'Lucatransiius Glow-bringer, the survey classifying anomalous cold in shaft eight as vein depletion — even as fire-core output dropped forty percent across two seasons. The survey suppressed evidence that something was consuming heat before harvest. The colony could not afford reduced output without losing passage through the Drowned Ledge. The forty-percent figure appears in multiple sources; I note it without the usual reservation because the ice-memory thermal record at that depth is unusually legible and confirms a decline of that approximate magnitude.
    
    ## Students
    
    - **Veil-render Seciae~**, whom Alnae~ Oss trained in the Crystalline Spiral. Seciae~ later developed techniques combining aurora-crystals with fire-cores. The relationship fractured after the Great Thaw; accounts agree they continued working together, though the nature of that collaboration had changed.
    - **Gilt-Hand Yeaiu qi'Gleam**, taught navigation in her youth. Alnae~ Oss called her "student" decades later — and entrusted her, in the end, with understanding what the navigation meant.
    - **☽'Saetacaeia-Viamana~**, a later student taught three forbidden magics: ice-memory reading, raw aurora channeling without crystal mediation, and the Crystalline Spiral. Alnae~ Oss warned her that what was learned could not be unlearned. ☽'Saetacaeia-Viamana~ would later use the third path — the reversed Spiral — to seal the Omega Obelisk, surrendering all three magics in the process.
    
    ## Death
    
    Alnae~ Oss died beneath Terrace Momiou confronting the corrupted fire-core her Order had buried there. When the corruption emerged, she pressed her scarred flippers to the gallery wall and offered acknowledgment rather than denial — feeding the hunger something it could not corrupt. The corrupted fire-core diminished but did not die. Her death bought time for Yeaiu qi'Gleam to retrieve the Compass of Crystal and complete the work.
    
    Her final lesson crystallized into the deep ice: *Light stored against the Long Dark.* I have read the impression. It is there.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771578741544_0", anchor: "she discovered both the Dreaming Tooth", text: "\"Discovered.\" The Dreaming Tooth was carved from the jawbone of the orca dead god — I established this in my annotation on the relic. An orca-divine artifact does not wander into Nightshelf tunnels unaided. Either it was placed before the colony was founded, or those tunnels intersect something older than ☽'scar Ramtatus~. The entry says \"discovered\" because I could not determine which. The ice at that stratum is illegible in ways I associate with deliberate erasure, not age.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771578741544_1", anchor: "interpreting the silence of vast, patient presences entombed there as doctrinal instruction", text: "She pressed her flippers to ice old enough to hold impressions from before penguin civilization and decided what answered was doctrine. The Foundation Depths contain strata from the same era. What is preserved there does not instruct. It watches. The Mandatum∴absconditu — survival through secrecy — may be sound policy. That it was dictated by something that predates penguins and has its own reasons for wanting them silent is not addressed in any version of Nightshelf scripture I have found.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771578741544_2", anchor: "The forty-percent figure appears in multiple sources", text: "I flagged this same number in my ☽'scar Ramtatus~ entry as a guild-master rounding — a figure shaped for council consumption. The thermal record at depth does confirm approximate magnitude. Guild-masters can be right for the wrong reasons. I owe them that much.", type: :correction, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771578741544_3", anchor: "The survey suppressed evidence that something was consuming heat before harvest", text: "This sentence does more work than anything else in the entry. The economic framing — Accord volumes, passage rights — is accurate but functions as camouflage. The corruption network operates through cold, not consumption. What feeds on geothermal heat? Neither Alnae~ Oss nor the young Lucatransiius named it. The survey they co-signed is preserved in administrative ice. I have read it. The word they used was \"dissipation.\" Dissipation does not leave scorch marks on shaft walls.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771578741544_4", anchor: "The relationship fractured after the Great Thaw", text: "My temporal annotation on Seciae~ identified a contradiction placing the dagger's forging in the Clever Ice Age while dating Seciae~'s emergence to the Great Thaw. If the earlier dating is correct, Seciae~ was not Alnae~ Oss's student — she was her predecessor's. The word \"fractured\" may describe a revelation, not a disagreement.", type: :pedantic, display: :popout
